From fa1ab8bfe9847fa660722351d4afa080108faa48 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 17:50:30 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] feat(post): per-operation smoothing, opt-in, in every
 mill dialect

A document-wide "Smoothing per operation" post option (#616), off by
default (byte-identical output). On, each operation states its ask -
a finishing op its own tolerance, a roughing op a fifth of the stock
it leaves (0.01-0.25 mm) - as PARAM Smoothing / SmoothingMode, and the
posts write their control's words after the preamble and undo them at
the section end:

- Tormach/LinuxCNC G64 P<tol> (back to the header's P after)
- Fanuc G5.1 Q1 / Q0 (no R level: control-version dependent)
- Haas G187 P3|P1 E<tol> / G187
- Siemens CYCLE832(<tol>,_FINISH|_ROUGH,1) / CYCLE832()
- Heidenhain ISO G62 T<tol> / G62
- Mazak: named once, no guessed word

Saved as the additive `smoothing` project key; undoable through
SetPostOptions; a checkbox under the post picker (mill posts).
Pinned by tests/smoothing.rs (4).

Fixes #616

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
