From e609a6ee9cb3dc487d7d43f5601216139930e21e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 18:13:01 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] fix(post): smoothing asks are bounded - Fanuc names it,
 finish asks half, rough never over a fifth

Review of #635:
1. Fanuc's G5.1 Q1 states no tolerance, so it could not hold the op's
   ask: the post names it once and writes nothing (like Mazak), until a
   bounded form is stated per control (#614).
2. The rough ask is stock x 0.2 capped at 0.25 mm with NO floor - the
   old 0.01 mm floor was 25-100% of a 0.01-0.04 mm allowance.
3. The finish ask is half the op's tolerance: the path is verified at
   the tolerance and the control's deviation stacks on it (1.5x, not 2x).
4. Tests: undo/redo of the switch, the project key round-trip (and no
   key when off), and the reset before the program end.
Also: the Heidenhain comment names ISO G62; Tormach's header and reset
share one blending constant.

