diff --git a/docs/decisions/616-smoothing.md b/docs/decisions/616-smoothing.md
index 70aadc50a..595dba4a9 100644
--- a/docs/decisions/616-smoothing.md
+++ b/docs/decisions/616-smoothing.md
@@ -8,20 +8,24 @@ Requested by @spikeypineapple (#616): smoothing modes differ per control, and th
   - **Why opt-in:** several controls need a paid option for smoothing (Fanuc's AI contour control), and a word an unequipped control rejects is worse than none. It also keeps the golden programs unchanged.
   - **Persistence:** saved as the additive `smoothing` project key, absent when off, the same pattern as `skip_stops` / `per_op_files`. It's a checkbox under the post picker for every mill post, undoable via `SetPostOptions`.
 - **The ask per operation** (`app::smoothing::of`):
-  - **Finish:** an op stating a contour `tolerance` and leaving no stock (Contour, Chamfer2D, Finish3D, Contour5D, Parallel5D, Swarf, AdvancedSwarf, RotaryContour) asks its tolerance, with a 0.01 mm floor if it states none.
-  - **Rough:** an op leaving stock (Contour with leave, Pocket, Adaptive2D, Offset2D, Slot, Circular, Bore, Pocket3D, RotaryOffset, MultiAxisRough) asks **stock_to_leave × 0.2, clamped to 0.01–0.25 mm**. That's a fifth of the allowance, so a rounded corner never eats more than 20 % of what the finish pass will remove, capped at 0.25 mm. Dropped: a direct stock-to-leave = tolerance mapping, which would let a 0.5 mm-leave rough round corners by the whole allowance.
+  - **Finish:** an op stating a contour `tolerance` and leaving no stock (Contour, Chamfer2D, Finish3D, Contour5D, Parallel5D, Swarf, AdvancedSwarf, RotaryContour) asks **half its tolerance** (0.01 mm stated tolerance if it states none).
+    - **Why half (review of #635):** the path is already generated and verified at the op's tolerance, and the control's deviation stacks on top. Asking the whole tolerance again would let the part sit about 2× tol from the verified path; half keeps the stack at 1.5× tol.
+  - **Rough:** an op leaving stock (Contour with leave, Pocket, Adaptive2D, Offset2D, Slot, Circular, Bore, Pocket3D, RotaryOffset, MultiAxisRough) asks **stock_to_leave × 0.2, capped at 0.25 mm**, and never more than that fifth.
+    - **No floor:** the first version floored at 0.01 mm, which was 25–100 % of a 0.01–0.04 mm allowance (review of #635). A thin allowance now asks tight.
+    - **Why a fifth:** a rounded corner never eats more than 20 % of what the finish pass will remove.
+    - **Dropped:** a direct stock-to-leave = tolerance mapping, which would let a 0.5 mm-leave rough round corners by the whole allowance.
   - **Nothing:** drilling, tapping, probing, threading, facing and the lathe kinds.
 - **Words per dialect**, each from the control's public programming documentation. Each is written after the section preamble and undone at the section end, so no tolerance leaks into the next op:
 
   | Post | On | Off |
   |---|---|---|
   | Tormach / LinuxCNC | `G64 P<tol>` | `G64 P0.001` / `P0.025` (the header's) |
-  | Fanuc | `G5.1 Q1` | `G5.1 Q0` |
+  | Fanuc | one note "SMOOTHING NOT WRITTEN - G5.1 STATES NO TOLERANCE" | nothing |
   | Haas | `G187 P3 E<tol>` (finish) / `G187 P1 E<tol>` (rough) | `G187` |
   | Siemens 840D | `CYCLE832(<tol>,_FINISH\|_ROUGH,1)` | `CYCLE832()` |
   | Heidenhain (ISO) | `G62 T<tol>` | `G62` |
   | Mazak | one note "SMOOTHING NOT WRITTEN - NO MAZAK FORM STATED" | nothing |
 
-- **Fanuc R level not written:** `G5.1 Q1 R<1-10>`'s R range is control-version dependent (as the requester noted), so only Q1/Q0 is written. A machine-file or post property for the R level can follow with #614 (the Doosan DNM), whose sample program will show the range that control accepts.
+- **Fanuc writes nothing yet (review of #635):** `G5.1 Q1` states no tolerance (the deviation is the control's own parameter, and `R<1-10>` is version dependent), so it can't be held to the op's ask. It is named once, like Mazak. A bounded Fanuc form (an R level mapped from a machine-stated table) can follow with #614 (the Doosan DNM).
 - **Mazak named, not guessed:** no smoothing form is stated from public Mazak documentation yet, and a guessed word could alarm the control.
 - **Not done here:** the lathe post (Fanuc Lathe writes no smoothing; the option isn't offered for it), and a per-op override (the ask is derived; an explicit per-op field can follow if wanted).

From ede835925093c9fbb37bd3042ef5eb92df860f62 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 09:35:07 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] fix(post): smoothing is read from each operation's own
 setup

The per-op smoothing ask was gated on the ACTIVE setup's post options,
while "Skip pauses and homes" (#389) is read from each op's own setup - so
with Setup1 smoothing and Setup2 not, posting with Setup1 active smoothed
Setup2's ops too. Now read per op from op.setup, like skip_stops. Found
by the delta review of #635 after main's per-setup post options landed.

Pinned by setup_post_options::smoothing_follows_each_ops_own_setup_not_the_active_one
(fails on the old gate: both setups' pockets smooth with Setup1 active).

Refs #616

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX
---
 crates/app/src/posting.rs              | 12 +++++--
 crates/app/tests/setup_post_options.rs | 43 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 52 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/crates/app/src/posting.rs b/crates/app/src/posting.rs
index 0a51c0fa5..0b7024081 100644
--- a/crates/app/src/posting.rs
+++ b/crates/app/src/posting.rs
@@ -831,9 +831,15 @@ pub fn op_streams(world: &World) -> Result<Vec<(String, Vec<cnc::Record>)>, Stri
             part_unload,
             part_transfer,
             probe_tol,
-            // #616: the op's smoothing ask, only when the document
-            // turned smoothing on (off: byte-identical output).
-            smoothing: if post_options(world).smoothing { crate::smoothing::of(&op.params) } else { None },
+            // #616: the op's smoothing ask, only when its OWN setup's
+            // post options turn smoothing on (off: byte-identical output) -
+            // read per op like "Skip pauses and homes" (#389), never from
+            // whichever setup happens to be active.
+            smoothing: if crate::setup_post_options::of(world, op.setup.as_deref()).smoothing {
+                crate::smoothing::of(&op.params)
+            } else {
+                None
+            },
             coolant: op.coolant,
             // "Skip pauses and homes" (#110) mutes every after-action
             // at post; the ops keep their choices. Entries ride it (#155).
